    <section class="wz-legal-section" lang="en" dir="ltr">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="wz-legal-meta">Last updated: 25 September 2026</p>
      <p>Shabbik is an Arabic crossword game. You can play without any account, and we never ask for your real name, email address or phone number.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>To learn which questions are hard and which are easy, the app sends anonymous gameplay events, such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>opening a question, solving it and how long that took, or leaving it unsolved;</li>
        <li>using a help (revealing a letter, removing letters, …);</li>
        <li>finishing a level, with the time taken and the stars earned.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These events carry a <strong>random device id</strong> the app creates when it is installed. It is not linked to you or to the advertising identifier, and we use it only to count distinct players. Events are deleted automatically after 180 days.</p>

      <h2>Username and leaderboards (optional)</h2>
      <p>If you choose a username in the app, we store that username, your avatar icon and your scores: points, levels and words solved, streak, daily game times and badges. <strong>Your username, avatar and scores are shown to other players</strong> on the leaderboards. A random key for your profile is kept in your iCloud Keychain; the server stores only a hash of it. Your profile is linked to your phone so we can notify you when someone passes your time in the daily puzzle (if notifications are on). You can permanently delete your profile and its scores at any time from the “ملفي” (profile) page in the app. We may rename an offensive username or hide it from the leaderboards.</p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>The game is free and paid for by adverts, served by <strong>Google AdMob</strong>: a banner at the bottom of some screens, an occasional advert between questions, sometimes one when you return to the app, and optional videos you can watch for coins.</p>
      <p>To show and measure adverts and to prevent fraud, Google's software in the app collects from your device: your IP address (which may be used to estimate your approximate location), device type and operating system, how you interact with adverts, and the <strong>advertising identifier</strong> (IDFA) if you allow it. Google handles this data under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>; it explains <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how it uses data from partner apps</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Tracking is your choice.</strong> iOS asks you once whether the app may track you. If you allow it, the advertising identifier is used to show adverts matched to your interests. If you decline, you still see adverts, but they are not personalised. You can change this at any time in Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Tracking. We never link the advertising identifier to your game profile or to gameplay events.</p>
      <p>In the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom, only non-personalised adverts are shown at present.</p>
      <p>The app keeps a count of the adverts you have seen today on your phone only, to respect the daily limit.</p>

      <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We never ask for your email, a password, your phone number or your location. (What Google receives to show adverts is described above.)</li>
        <li>No third-party analytics: the gameplay events above go to our own server only.</li>
        <li>Achievements use Game Center; Apple handles that data under its own policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about your privacy: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a></p>
    </section>
